# Template for /etc/booking-buddy/credentials.env — copy, fill in, then install it:
#
#   sudo install -d -m 700 -o root -g root /etc/booking-buddy
#   sudo install -m 600 -o root -g root bot/systemd/credentials.env.example \
#       /etc/booking-buddy/credentials.env
#   sudoedit /etc/booking-buddy/credentials.env
#
# The unit reads it as EnvironmentFile=-/etc/booking-buddy/credentials.env, so it
# stays optional: with no such file the service runs exactly as before, off
# auth.json. It exists because CourtReserve drops a saved session every few
# weeks, and without credentials the next run falls through to the interactive
# manual-login prompt that a Type=oneshot unit has no TTY for.
#
# systemd reads this file as root before dropping privileges, so it must be
# root:root mode 600 — install.sh warns about anything else.
#
# A credential login that fails throws (credential-login-failed); it never falls
# back to the prompt. Leaving REPLACE_ME in place therefore fails loudly at the
# next run rather than hanging, but it is still not a working login. Only the
# username is ever written to the log. Rotate by editing the installed file and
# restarting the service.
#
# Single-quote a value that contains spaces or a # ; unquoted values are taken
# literally up to end of line.
COURTRESERVE_USERNAME=REPLACE_ME
COURTRESERVE_PASSWORD=REPLACE_ME